---
description: Explains where and how to cancel a reservation, including the deadline.
type: predicate
min_probability: 0.5
---
<system>
Does the policy explicitly tell a member where to cancel a desk reservation, which action completes the cancellation, and when cancellation is allowed?

The condition is satisfied only when all three details are present:
- Where to go, such as a named page or service desk.
- What to do there to cancel the booking.
- The cancellation deadline or an explicit statement that cancellation is always allowed.

A statement that cancellations are possible is insufficient. Releasing a reservation after a missed check-in does not explain how a member can cancel it. Evaluate only the supplied policy; do not infer missing steps from how other reservation systems work.
</system>

